@*
    Client-side validation without jQuery.

    aspnet-client-validation reads the same data-val-* attributes the tag helpers already emit, so
    every asp-validation-for and asp-validation-summary in the pages is unchanged - what changes is
    who reads them. jQuery was in this project for this partial and nothing else; no script of ours
    ever called it.

    Unlike jquery.validate.unobtrusive this does not start itself, so site.js bootstraps it. That
    call lives there rather than in an inline block here on purpose: an inline script is one more
    thing a Content-Security-Policy has to carry a nonce for, and the colour-mode block in _Layout
    is already the one exception worth paying for.

    Server-side validation is unaffected and remains the thing that actually decides. This partial
    only spares somebody a round trip.
*@
<environment include="Development">
    <script src="~/lib/aspnet-client-validation/dist/aspnet-validation.js"></script>
</environment>
<environment exclude="Development">
    <script src="~/lib/aspnet-client-validation/dist/aspnet-validation.min.js" asp-append-version="true"></script>
</environment>
